\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  O how shall I receive Thee,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Now great Thee, Lord, aright?
\par All nations long to see Thee,
\par My hope, my heart's delight!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O kindle, Lord most holy,
\par Thy lamp within my breast;
\par To do in spirit lowly
\par All that may please Thee best.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Thy Zion strews before Thee,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Palm branches fresh and fair;
\par My heart in joy would bring Thee
\par An anthem I'll prepare.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par My soul puts off its sadness
\par Thy glories to proclaim;
\par With all its strength and gladness
\par It would but serve Thy name!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. And when I'm filled with sorrow,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Thou com'st to set me free;
\par I see a bright tomorrow,
\par For Thou, Lord, art with me!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Thy glory Thou dost give me,
\par A treasure safe on high
\par That will not fail nor leave me
\par As earthly riches fly.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. Love caus'd Thy incarnation,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Love brought Thee down to me.
\par Thy thirst for my salvation
\par Procured my liberty.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par O love beyond expression
\par That led Thee to embrace
\par In love all love excelling,
\par Our lost and fallen race!
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

